extends layout.pug

block content-header
  link(rel='stylesheet', type='text/css', href='/style/downloads.css')

block content-block
  .page-content
    h1 Downloads
    p Every release of GNIS-LD is available as a complete database export — roughly fourteen million triples of N-Triples you can load into any triple store. The current release is always served live at the SPARQL endpoint and exportable from the #[a(href='/data') data] endpoint.

    h2 Release cadence
    p GNIS-LD tracks the USGS GNIS domestic names data on a #[strong quarterly] cadence: each quarter the latest USGS files are converted through the #[a(href='https://github.com/DataONEorg/usgs-triplifier' target='_blank') triplifier pipeline], loaded into the live endpoint, and archived here automatically. Feature identifiers never change between releases — a new quarter adds new features and updates descriptive properties, so links made against any release keep resolving against every later one. Releases are also recorded in the dataset's #[a(href='/docs#metadata') VoID/DCAT metadata], so the archive below is machine-discoverable.
    p Each release ships in two parts. The main dump is a faithful conversion of exactly what USGS currently publishes. Its #[strong historical companion] carries the last-known records of features USGS has stopped shipping — typed #[code usgs:HistoricalFeature], with #[code gnis:lastAppearedIn] pointing at the release that last contained them — and the live endpoint loads both, which is how feature URIs stay resolvable forever.

    h2 Release archive
    if releases && releases.length
      table.release-table
        thead
          tr
            th Release
            th Published
            th Triples
            th Size
            th
        tbody
          each release, i in releases
            tr(class=i === 0 ? 'current' : undefined)
              td
                | #{release.id}
                if i === 0
                  span.current-chip Current
              td #{release.published}
              td #{release.triples}
              td #{release.size}
              td.dl-cell
                a.dl-btn(href=release.url target='_blank') Download
                if release.historical
                  a.dl-historical(href=release.historical.url target='_blank') + historical (#{release.historical.size})
    else
      p No archived releases yet — the current release is always available from the #[a(href='/data') live export].

    p.archive-note Archives are N-Triples, uncompressed. For loading instructions, see the #[a(href='/integrations') integrations guide]; for how releases link together, see #[a(href='/docs#lineage') querying across lineage].
